From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: simple: add a tuning file for the GC02M2

Like the OV5648 before it, the GC02M2 falls back to uncalibrated.yaml and
has its black level re-guessed from the histogram on every exposure change.

Pin the pedestal. The sensor's black level correction targets 64 in its
10-bit output (dark frames on a PineTab 2 average 64.6), which is 4096 in
the 16-bit units the tuning file uses.

No colour correction matrix, for the same reason as the OV5648: it has to
be measured, not borrowed.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/meson.build
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
 
 conf_files = files([
+    'gc02m2.yaml',
     'ov5648.yaml',
     'uncalibrated.yaml',
 ])
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/ipa/simple/data/gc02m2.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: CC0-1.0
+%YAML 1.1
+---
+version: 1
+algorithms:
+  - BlackLevel:
+      # The sensor's black level correction targets 64 in its 10-bit
+      # output (dark frames on a PineTab 2 average 64.6), so the pedestal
+      # is 64/1023 -> 4096 in the 16-bit units this file uses.
+      blackLevel: 4096
+  - Awb:
+  # A colour correction matrix belongs here once it has been measured
+  # against a colour chart with utils/tuning:
+  #
+  #   - Ccm:
+  #       ccms:
+  #         - ct: 6500
+  #           ccm: [ ... ]
+  - Adjust:
+  - Agc:
+...
